# pdfminer.six CVEs — pdfplumber pins the version, cannot upgrade independently.
# Risk: pdfminer processes trusted invoice PDFs uploaded by authenticated users only.
# Review date: 2026-07-09
CVE-2025-64512
CVE-2025-70559

# starlette CVEs requiring starlette ≥1.0 — FastAPI 0.x depends on starlette 0.4x.
# FastAPI has not yet released a 1.0 that uses starlette 1.x.
# These CVEs relate to SSRF via UNC paths (Windows-only, not applicable to our Linux
# containers) and DoS via form limits (mitigated by nginx rate limiting upstream).
# Review date: 2026-07-09
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283
CVE-2025-62727

# pyasn1 CVE — python-jose pins pyasn1<0.5.0, cannot upgrade independently.
# DoS via unbounded recursion — mitigated by request size limits at nginx.
# Review date: 2026-07-09
CVE-2026-30922

# pyasn1 CVEs (2026-07-22) — python-jose pins pyasn1<0.5.0, cannot upgrade independently.
# DoS via crafted ASN.1 values — mitigated by request size limits at nginx + authenticated-only access.
# NOTE: CVE-2026-59884 (same family, HIGH) has a fix in pyasn1>=0.6.4 — upgraded in Dockerfile.
#       These two remain unfixed upstream as of 2026-08-01.
CVE-2026-59885
CVE-2026-59886

# msgpack CVE — upgraded to 1.2.1 in Dockerfile but base image retains 1.1.2 metadata.
# OOB read on Unpacker reuse — not exploitable in our usage (we use msgpack for Redis serialization only).
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools CVE — upgraded to 83.0.0 in Dockerfile but base python:3.12-slim ships with 70.3.0.
# Path traversal in PackageIndex — not exploitable (we don't use setuptools at runtime, only during build).
CVE-2025-47273

# openssl CVE-2026-14456 — DoS via unbounded memory growth in QUIC server.
# Not applicable: we do not run an OpenSSL QUIC server. nginx terminates TLS externally.
# Fix available in openssl 3.5.7 — apt-get upgrade pulls it when Debian backport is available.
# Review date: 2026-08-23
CVE-2026-14456

# util-linux CVEs (CVE-2026-53612/53613/53614) — TOCTOU and nosuid/noexec bypass in SUID mount(8).
# Not applicable: containers run without SUID mount, no privileged mount operations.
# Fix available in util-linux 2.41.5 — apt-get upgrade pulls it when Debian backport is available.
# Review date: 2026-08-23
CVE-2026-53612
CVE-2026-53613
CVE-2026-53614

# urllib3 CVE-2026-97687 (HTTPS proxy TLS override) + CVE-2026-97689 (DoS via chunk parser).
# ALREADY FIXED in the image: urllib3 is pinned to >=2.8.0 in requirements.txt + the Dockerfile
# upgrade line, and the built image contains ONLY urllib3-2.8.0.dist-info (verified by a local
# `docker build` + `find / -name 'urllib3-*.dist-info'` → single 2.8.0 entry; runtime import
# reports 2.8.0). trivy-action@master's advisory DB still reports these against a phantom "2.7.0"
# even though the scanned file table lists urllib3-2.8.0.dist-info — a scanner/DB artifact, not a
# real exposure. Ignoring with the fix in place. Review date: 2026-10-03.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
